      "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{44x+48}{(x+6)(x-3)(x+2)} & =\\frac{A}{(x+6)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+6)(x-3)(x+2)$ gives\n\n$$\n44x+48=A(x-3)(x+2)+B(x+6)(x+2)+C(x+6)(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-6$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}44(-6)+48 & =A(-6-3)(-6+2) \\\\  & \\,+B(-6+6)(-6+2) \\\\  & \\,+C(-6+6)(-6-3) \\\\ -264+48 & =A(36) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-216}{36} \\\\ A & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}44(3)+48 & =A(3-3)(3+2) \\\\  & \\,+B(3+6)(3+2) \\\\  & \\,+C(3+6)(3-3) \\\\ 132+48 & =B(45) \\\\ B & =\\frac{180}{45} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-2$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}44(-2)+48 & =A(-2-3)(-2+2) \\\\  & \\,+B(-2+6)(-2+2) \\\\  & \\,+C(-2+6)(-2-3) \\\\ -88+48 & =C(-20) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-40}{-20} \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{44x+48}{(x+6)(x-3)(x+2)}=-\\frac{6}{(x+6)}+\\frac{4}{(x-3)}+\\frac{2}{(x+2)}.\n$$",
